WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.620
2014 saw the release of a little movie about
a retired assassin on a quest to avenge his

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.120
dog.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.920
Thanks to the star power of Keanu Reeves and
some killer fight choreography, John Wick

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.660
became a phenomenon, and a franchise was born.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.140
Here's what we know so far about Mr. Wick's
past, his criminal career, his motivations…

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:19.580
and what he intends to do next.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.760
Not much is known about John Wick's early
life, but we do learn in John Wick: Chapter

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:28.660
3: — Parabellum that "John Wick" is not
his real name and that he's an orphan.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.400
When he's desperate for assistance after being
declared excommunicado, he goes to see the

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.600
Director, and during their meeting it's revealed
to the audience that his real name is Jardani

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.460
Jovanovich, and that his ancestry is Belarusian.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:45.660
This heritage, and John's status as the last
of his particular tribe, is enough to ensure

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.480
him safe passage from New York City to Casablanca.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:49.720
"So tell me Jardani.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.120
What do you really want?"

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.960
In addition to the combat training he presumably
underwent as a young man via the Director,

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.860
at some point in his life Wick may have entered
the United States Marine Corps.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:07.200
The tattoo across his upper back is Latin
for "Fortune Favors the Bold," the motto of

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.650
the 3rd Marine Regiment stationed in Hawaii,
which itself is likely a nod to Keanu Reeves'

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:13.200
own Hawaiian heritage.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.930
The John Wick films don't tell us exactly
when or how John became a killer for hire,

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:23.640
but they do suggest certain things — namely
that Wick's chief mentor may have been Marcus,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.920
his friend and fellow assassin who ultimately
takes a contract to kill him in the first

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:27.480
film.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.160
What we do know for sure is that John was
a natural hitman, and quickly developed a

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:34.100
reputation that earned him the nickname "Baba
Yaga".

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.990
He was the boogeyman for the most dangerous
people in the world, and he could kill with

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:42.200
tremendous efficiency in just about any way
he had to — including, famously, with a

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:42.780
pencil.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.180
At some point during his career as a sought
after and feared assassin, John did some kind

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.720
of favor for his friend Sofia, which called
for her to offer him a blood oath marker which

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.320
he could later cash in.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:59.000
At an unknown point in his career, Wick came
under the employ of Viggo Tarasov, a mob boss

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.270
with big ambitions.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:04.960
Then, though the life he'd chosen was supposed
to be permanent, Wick approached Tarasov and

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.700
"asked to leave" because he was in love with
a woman.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.280
Tarasov agreed to let Wick retire, but only
if he performed "a job no one could have pulled

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:11.820
off."

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.040
Tarasov does not go into specifics in the
films, but Wick's legendary "Impossible Task"

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.200
was apparently a series of assassinations,
and "the bodies he buried that day" paved

00:02:21.202 --> 00:02:25.730
the way for Tarasov and his family to rise
up through the ranks of organized crime.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:30.880
Having accomplished his impossible task, Wick
was allowed to retire from his life as a contract

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.880
killer, and Tarasov became one of the most
powerful men in the crime world.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:39.811
As we learn in John Wick 2, during the "Impossible
Task," Wick also sought the help of his friend

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:43.860
Santino D'Antonio, who secured a blood oath
marker from Wick for his trouble.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:49.620
After the Impossible Task was completed, Wick
left the world of crime, going so far as to

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:52.520
bury his guns and remaining gold under concrete
in his basement.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.160
He married Helen, and the two settled into
a happy life together.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.220
That happiness, unfortunately, was not to
last.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.360
At some point in the course of their marriage,
Helen fell ill.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:07.040
The illness was terminal, and she died shortly
before the events of the first John Wick film.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.430
The films rarely elaborate on Helen or her
illness, but we of course know that her death

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.709
greatly impacted John, to the point that he's
willing to stay alive if only to remember

00:03:15.709 --> 00:03:19.380
her, so that everything he did in order to
have a life with her will be worthwhile.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.920
We can also infer that Helen was a wise woman
who knew that death was coming, and also knew

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.900
that her husband would not handle the grieving
process well alone.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:31.820
To ease his pain, at some point before her
death she arranged for a puppy to be delivered

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:33.220
to his doorstep to help him move on.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.440
The main events of the first John Wick film
begin just days after Helen's death, when

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:42.160
several years have apparently passed since
John's retirement as an assassin.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:47.099
We can infer this because Viggo Tarasov's
young son, Iosef seems to be the only denizen

00:03:47.099 --> 00:03:50.099
of the criminal underworld who doesn't know
who John is.

00:03:50.099 --> 00:03:54.370
We know that because Iosef and his friends
decide, after seeing Wick's classic Ford Mustang,

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:56.800
to stage a home invasion and steal the car.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.370
They also kill Wick's new puppy, Daisy, in
the process… and make the mistake of leaving

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:02.780
Wick alive.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:07.080
When Iosef takes the Mustang to a chop shop
to have its VIN changed, word begins to spread

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:11.709
in the underworld of the sin he's just committed,
while John digs up his guns and gold and prepares

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:13.430
to go on a quest for vengeance.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:17.739
Viggo berates his son for what he's done,
but still prepares to go to war with Wick,

00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:20.880
even taking out a contract to have Wick killed
in the process.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.900
Some of the most talented assassins in the
world try and fail to stop Wick as he burns

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:29.560
through the Tarasov family in New York City,
eventually killing both Iosef and Viggo.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.750
Eventually, the vendetta ends at the chop
shop of Viggo's brother Abram, where Wick

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.490
retrieves his car and makes peace.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:39.400
He returns home and buries his guns once more.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:43.530
John returns home with a new, unnamed dog
and tries to move on with his life, but his

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:48.160
peace is quickly interrupted by Santino, who
arrives to cash in on the marker John had

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:53.270
given him years before in exchange for Santino's
assistance with the Impossible Task.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:57.830
John initially rejects Santino's demand that
he honor the marker, and Santino retaliates

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.810
by destroying John's home.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:03.800
John journeys to New York City once again
and heads to the Continental, a hotel that

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:08.250
exists as a sanctuary for criminals with strict
rules governed by the underworld.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:12.840
After some encouragement from Winston, the
hotel's proprietor, he agrees to meet with

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:13.840
Santino.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.940
Santino wants to hire John to assassinate
his sister Gianna, who is about to ascend

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:22.680
to a seat at the High Table, a council of
crime lords that rules over the whole underworld.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:26.410
With his sister out of the way, Santino could
claim the High Table seat for himself, but

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:30.110
he can't kill her, because that would spark
a war among assassins.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:33.520
John reluctantly agrees and travels to Italy
to kill Gianna.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:37.740
When he arrives and meets Gianna in secret
during her coronation festivities, we learn

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.260
that the two are old friends.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:44.070
Knowing that John is bound by a blood oath
to carry out the hit, Gianna slits her wrists

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.500
in an effort to die on her own terms.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.380
As she loses consciousness, John puts a bullet
in her head.

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:54.380
Even as he was honoring the Marker by killing
Gianna, John was under surveillance from Santino's

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:56.320
mute bodyguard, Ares.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:00.840
In the catacombs beneath Gianna's compound,
Santino's henchmen attack John.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:04.640
Santino always intended to double cross his
old friend and tie up all possible loose ends

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:07.060
connected to his coup against his sister.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:11.680
John fights his way out and returns to New
York City, where he learns that Santino has

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:16.410
taken out a $7 million contract against him
as a public show of vengeance for his sister's

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:16.960
death.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:21.620
Another one of Gianna's loyal bodyguards,
Cassian, attempts to cash in on this contract

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:26.320
and avenge her, but John defeats him in combat
and ultimately seeks refuge with the Bowery

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:30.560
King, who grants him a gun with seven bullets
which he can use to seek vengeance against

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.120
Santino.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:36.240
John fights his way through Santino's guards,
but Santino himself seeks refuge in the Continental,

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:40.080
where one of the chief rules is that no blood
can be spilled on hotel grounds.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:44.940
John breaks this cardinal rule and shoots
Santino in the head in the hotel's lounge,

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.520
forcing Winston to declare him "excommunicado."

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:52.319
In honor of their friendship, Winston grants
John one hour to flee before a contract on

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.450
his life takes effect.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.720
"Tick tock Mr. Wick."

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:00.900
Even before his hour-long grace period is
up, other assassins are determined to kill

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:01.480
John Wick.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:06.040
Seeking refuge, John retrieves a crucifix
and one last marker from a dummy book in the

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:09.000
New York Public Library, and visits the Director.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.250
She "tears his ticket" and brands him with
the crucifix.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:16.820
This gesture is enough to get him to Casablanca,
where he finds Sofia and uses the marker she

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:18.500
gave him to ask for a favor.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:23.680
That favor is ultimately a journey to find
the Elder, the only person left who can restore

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:27.100
his status with the High Table and allow him
to continue living his life.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:31.100
John explains that he wants to keep living
so that he can carry on the memory of his

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:33.740
wife Helen, and the Elder offers him a deal.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:37.960
If John will show his loyalty by killing Winston
and continuing to serve the High Table as

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.250
an assassin, he can go on living.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:44.140
John agrees to this deal, severing his own
ring finger and giving his wedding ring to

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:45.620
the Elder as a sign of devotion.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:50.620
While John is overseas attempting to restore
his status with the High Table, an Adjudicator

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:54.870
arrives in New York to dispatch justice on
behalf of the High Table for the wrongs done

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.060
in John Wick: Chapter 2.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:00.380
To carry this out, the Adjudicator recruits
Zero, a loyal assassin, and they begin their

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:00.940
work.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:05.620
For his role in giving John a one-hour head
start, the Adjudicator tells Winston that

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:09.460
he has seven days to get his affairs in order
before being removed from the Continental.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.220
The Adjudicator then goes to the Director
and, in retribution for her role in letting

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:17.440
John escape, has Zero plunge a sword through
both of her hands.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.560
They then visit the Bowery King.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:24.500
As punishment for providing the gun and seven
bullets John used to kill Santino on Continental

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:29.520
grounds, the Adjudicator orders Zero to give
the Bowery King seven cuts with his sword.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.940
The Bowery King is severely wounded, but survives.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.240
John returns to New York City after his meeting
with the Elder, but his restoration to service

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:40.619
with the High Table will not be complete until
he kills Winston.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.780
With Zero's men in pursuit, both John and
Winston decide to deny their orders from the

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:45.320
Table.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:49.340
Winston will not step down as manager of the
Continental, and John will not kill his old

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:49.960
friend.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:54.420
In response, the Adjudicator orders the New
York Continental to be "deconsecrated", and

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:59.500
a squad of High Table enforcers arrive to
kill Winston, John, and everyone loyal to

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.100
them, including the Continental's concierge,
Charon.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:06.480
Though they initially struggle to fight off
the SWAT-like enforcers with their bulletproof

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:10.320
armor, John and Charon defeat the squad with
armor piercing rounds.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.260
John then goes on to battle Zero and his men,
narrowly walking away victorious.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:19.019
Winston, meanwhile, uses his defeat of the
High Table enforcers as leverage to parley

00:09:19.019 --> 00:09:23.029
with the Adjudicator, who decides to frame
the defense of the Continental as a "show

00:09:23.029 --> 00:09:24.720
of strength" from Winston.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:29.160
To prove his loyalty to the High Table, Winston
shoots John, who falls off the hotel roof.

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:34.660
The Adjudicator agrees to reconsecrate the
Contintental and restore Winston to power,

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:37.380
but when they look for John's body in the
alley, he's gone.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:42.640
The Adjudicator makes it clear that John remains
a threat to both Winston and to the High Table,

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:45.100
which Winston is all too aware of himself.

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:50.189
John, severely wounded but alive, is transported
to the Bowery King by his servants.

00:09:50.189 --> 00:09:54.610
The King, still suffering from his sword wounds
and struggling to walk, makes it clear that

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.310
he does not accept the punishment of the High
Table.

00:09:57.310 --> 00:10:01.369
The Bowery King declares that he's ready to
wage war against the Table for their attempt

00:10:01.369 --> 00:10:06.079
to remove him from his territory, and asks
John if he's also ready to fight back.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.040
John says that he is, setting the stage for
a confrontation.

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:14.279
Shortly after John Wick 3 was released, Lionsgate
confirmed that a fourth film in the franchise

00:10:14.279 --> 00:10:19.519
will arrive May 21, 2021, setting the stage
for the war between the Bowery and the High

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:20.100
Table.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.140
"You've got a nasty surprise comin'."

00:10:22.509 --> 00:10:24.660
